        "raw": "<p>had first GSF playthrough today: &nbsp;So first off, the ZK-19 Guardship. &nbsp;It reads &quot;Whenever Energy would be removed from an Opposition Ship in this sector other than a Guardship, reduce the amout reduced by two.&quot; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br />Is this a typo? &nbsp;Does it simply not mean what I think it means? &nbsp; Reduce the amount reduced by two? &nbsp; So... it takes 2 increased damage? &nbsp; We have a double-negative going on here. &nbsp; &nbsp;Or is it supposed to simply read &quot;reduce the amount by two&quot;, &nbsp;meaning effectively that all Opposition ships other than the guardship have 2 DR? &nbsp; That seems like how it is supposed to read.<br /><br />Also, what exactly counts as an opposition ship? &nbsp; Is it just the cards from the opposition ship deck (the red cards) &nbsp;or does that include the ships from the station decks too (red and orange cards). &nbsp;Do unengaged Orange cards flip cards from station decks during the Aftermath phase? &nbsp; &nbsp;Is the Flagship an Opposition ship? &nbsp;Does it flip cards during the Aftermath phase? &nbsp; If so, &nbsp;is it correct to say that once the flagship shows up, the only way to win the game is by destroying the Flagship?<br />&nbsp;</p>",
