      {
        "id": 105375,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-31T12:38:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Cool, &nbsp;that's pretty much how we were playing it. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, can I travel to a sector that I am already in? &nbsp;This might not seem like a big deal, but I was playing Kauchar's Claw and it sort of is.<br><br>Edit: &nbsp; &nbsp;and... &nbsp;can I engage as many opposition ships as I want? &nbsp;I initially assumed I can engage only once (choosing to be either a primary or secondary engager) but I am not seeing where it actually says that. &nbsp;Can I engage multiple ships? &nbsp;If myself an an allied strike force ship are in the same sector with say, 2 opposition ships, &nbsp;can I engage Opposition ship A as a Primary Engager and Opposition Ship B as a Secondary engager, while my ally engages B as a primary engager and A as a secondary engager? &nbsp;Could I engage both A and B as a primary engager (in both cases)? &nbsp; &nbsp;The only thing I see is that multiple strike force ships can't be primary engagers against the same enemy, &nbsp; I don't see anything that says a strike force ship cant be a primary engager against multiple opposition ships though.<br><br>If I have the Cloak Drive can I engage everything? &nbsp;Engage -travel to another sector, engage, travel to another sector, engage, travel to another sector, etc, until all Opposition ships are engaged, but I would only have to actually do battle against Opposition ships in the sector I end up in.</p>",
