        "raw": " \n[quote=\"awp832\"]\n \n\nI initially assumed I can engage only once (choosing to be either a primary or secondary engager) but I am not seeing where it actually says that. &nbsp;Can I engage multiple ships? &nbsp;If myself an an allied strike force ship are in the same sector with say, 2 opposition ships, &nbsp;can I engage Opposition ship A as a Primary Engager and Opposition Ship B as a Secondary engager, while my ally engages B as a primary engager and A as a secondary engager?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\nPage 9, second sentence under &quot;Engage Event&quot;\n<blockquote>\nA strike force ship can either engage as a primary engager or a secondary engager.\n</blockquote>\n&nbsp;\n\n[quote=\"awp832\"]\n\n&nbsp;Also, can I travel to a sector that I am already in? &nbsp;This might not seem like a big deal, but I was playing Kauchar&#39;s Claw and it sort of is.\n\n[/quote]\n\nHit and Run\n<blockquote>\nKharacgar&#39;s Claw may travel to another Sector.\n</blockquote>\nDeadly Focus\n<blockquote>\nKharachar&#39;s Claw and an Opposition Ship engaged with the Karachar&#39;s Claw travel to another Sector.\n</blockquote>\nNow I don&#39;t know if you can &quot;travel&quot; to the sector you are currently in or not (I don&#39;t think you can, since the travel event says &quot;you may move to another sector&quot;), but using Karachar&#39;s Claw makes you travel to another sector. Since traveling to the same sector is not traveling to another sector.\n\n&nbsp;\n<blockquote>\ncan I engage as many opposition ships as I want?\n</blockquote>\nNo, Strike Force Ships can only engage with one ship.\n",
